NAME
    echo - print arguments to standard output

SYNOPSIS
    echo [text...]

DESCRIPTION
    Prints all arguments joined by single spaces. Standard shell quoting
    applies before echo runs. Standard input is ignored.

    echo does not parse flags such as -n or -e; every argument is printed
    literally.

EXAMPLES
    echo hello world
    echo "$NAME"
    echo "line one" | sed s/one/two/

EXIT STATUS
    0   Always succeeds.

SEE ALSO
    cat(1), sed(1), awk(1)
